    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The parent registry lacks Qwen3MoeForCausalLM, so Config.from_directory rejects that architecture before model construction.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_76a7fb171b00482886735b17497e6765",
          "call_9e5f5e6655e745d79b1286d02fff0831",
          "call_f45fd0fe29b9469fbe1b3e72075aa30f"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "The new builder combines Qwen3-style normalized attention with the existing BlockSparseMLP and enables all-expert calibration rather than introducing new inference kernels.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_07cd83fdad164378a2b5d968c2a1888e",
          "call_1d7bc409230746fb8d5cb7e87bbb4930",
          "call_97b554b1e6594ba5953b476a05a9b454"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Registry dispatch now selects Qwen3MoeConfig and Qwen3MoeModel. The change supplies model assembly and calibration policy; it does not establish successful loading or generation for every checkpoint format.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5c6e15f005f64e2e9b3c9a5300b9c753",
          "call_07cd83fdad164378a2b5d968c2a1888e"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The earlier BlockSparseMLP entry records an all-expert fused-path shape mismatch. Fresh inspection finds that implementation unchanged and newly connected to Qwen3MoeModel; its conditional failure is recorded here.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_00bd8c686a644175a4ad9f392c727a9f"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Issue #29, \u201cAuto-YaRN for Qwen3? Maybe even set it dynamically?\u201d, requests scaling-policy changes. Its relationship here is inferred only from shared Qwen3/RoPE configuration; this patch delegates to the existing configuration helper.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_5d534736d451454d9f9b9a5b789c68b2",
          "call_07cd83fdad164378a2b5d968c2a1888e"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #35, \u201chumaneval.py: fix top_k type, remove rep_p, add qwen3\u201d, concerns sampling and evaluation. PR #4, \u201cchore: update config.py\u201d, proposes a spelling correction. Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate\u201d, reports extension loading, while issue #34, \u201ctorch._C._LinAlgError on last layer of quant\u201d, reports Cholesky failure. Any association with this task is inferred from Qwen3 terminology or shared inspected configuration/conversion files, not an explicit task reference.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6c193376451a43438dd637b008e49cae",
          "call_c7a1b26152254e42893b4113900f0017",
